<section class="method">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow">Method</div>
    <h2>From scattered records to a board-usable file &mdash; in four steps</h2>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step">
        <div class="n">I</div>
        <h3>Define the decision</h3>
        <p>Who will read the file, which request it answers, and the deadline that matters.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="n">II</div>
        <h3>Map request to evidence</h3>
        <p>Every buyer question linked to the record that answers it &mdash; owner, date, scope, source.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="n">III</div>
        <h3>Register the gaps</h3>
        <p>What is missing, expired or inconsistent &mdash; classified, prioritised and assigned.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="n">IV</div>
        <h3>Deliver the file</h3>
        <p>A buyer-readable evidence structure your CFO can defend in one meeting.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="note">The work is advisory. It does not replace legal advice, customs representation, accredited certification, independent assurance &mdash; or the legally responsible operator. That boundary is stated on every deliverable.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="method">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow">The framework</div>
    <h2>One published yardstick: the Supplier Evidence Maturity Model</h2>
    <p class="lead">Every review is graded against SEMM &mdash; five levels, from evidence that does not exist to a file that maintains itself. The methodology is public and citable, so a supplier, a buyer and an advisor can talk about the same file with the same words.</p>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="{{@site.url}}/supplier-evidence-maturity-model/">Read the SEMM framework &rarr;</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

